>> title: Bún Thịt Nướng
>> category: Rice, Beans & Grains
>> tags: pork, rice noodles, vietnamese, lemongrass, grill
>> counters: Phở & Bánh Mì
>> aka: bun thit nuong, bún thịt nướng, grilled pork vermicelli, grilled pork noodle bowl, vermicelli bowl, noodle bowl, bun bowl, cold noodle bowl, B1
>> pairs-with: nuoc-cham, do-chua
>> servings: 4
>> time: 2 hr 45 min
>> slack: narrow — sugar and fish sauce on thin pork goes from charred edges to burnt through fast, and the eight minutes over the fire is all of it

>> step: stir the marinade
Stir @lemongrass{3%stalks}(tender lower third, minced fine), @garlic{3%cloves}(minced), @granulated sugar{2%Tbs}(25 g), @fish sauce{2%Tbs}(30 mL) and @vegetable oil{1%Tbs}(15 mL) into a marinade.

>> step: marinate chilled 2 hr
Marinate @pork shoulder{1%lb}(450 g; sliced 1/4 inch across the grain) in @&(~1)marinade{} in the #fridge{} ~marinate{2%hr}.

>> step: grill 8 min, until the edges char
Grill @&(~1)pork{} over hot coals ~grill{8%min}, turning once, until the edges char and the sugar catches.

>> step: boil 4 min, rinse cold
Boil @rice vermicelli{6%oz}(170 g) in @water{3%qt}(2.8 L) ~boil{4%min}, then drain and rinse cold.

>> step: arrange the bowl, dress at the table
Arrange @&(~1)noodles{} over @lettuce{4%leaves}(shredded), @cucumber{1/2}(in matchsticks), @mint{1/2%cup} and @đồ chua{1/2%cup}(drained), lay @&(~2)grilled pork{} across the top, and finish with @roasted peanuts{1/4%cup}(chopped), @fried shallots{2%Tbs} and @nước chấm{1%cup} poured over at the table, then turned through with chopsticks until everything is wet.
